# Design Narrative
# Mechanic: Selfless Spirit is sacrificed to give friendly creatures indestructible before Anger of the Gods resolves.
# Forcing: Anger alone kills every creature. Sacrificing the Spirit first preserves two attackers while removing both blockers.
# AI behavior: The opponent has two blockers and no cards or abilities to change the board.
# Failure modes:
#   WIN = the Spirit protects both friendly attackers, Anger removes the blockers, and the survivors attack for five.
#   LOSE = Anger is cast before the Spirit's ability, destroying the attackers too.
#   TIMEOUT = sacrifice ability or board-wipe resolution did not complete.
# Card roles:
#   Selfless Spirit — protects the two attackers at the cost of itself.
#   Anger of the Gods — clears blockers while threatening friendly creatures.
#   Grizzly Bears and Centaur Courser — exact-five-power attackers.
#   Opposing Bears and Courser — blockers removed by the sweep.
# Protocol path: Sacrifice Spirit, resolve indestructible, cast Anger, attack.
[metadata]
